# Speech Coach engine freeze (mandatory)

Full protocol: `docs/speech-coach-engine-freeze.md`

## Frozen infrastructure (single owner each)

| Concern | Owner module |
|---------|----------------|
| Audio playback | `amy-voice-controller.ts` + `useAmyVoice()` |
| Microphone | `microphone-session-manager.ts` + `useSpeechRecognition()` |
| Dialogue | `lib/speech-coach/src/coach-dialogue.ts` |
| Memory | `lib/speech-coach/src/coach-memory.ts` |
| Learning journey | `lib/speech-coach/src/coach-journey.ts` |
| Audio warmup | `global-audio-warmup.ts` |
| Phonics playback | `phonics-player.ts` |

## Do NOT

- Rewrite architecture or replace ownership models
- Add alternate playback paths or duplicate session managers
- Call `new Audio()`, `audio.play()`, `MediaRecorder`, `getUserMedia`, `speechSynthesis`, or `AudioContext` from feature/UI code
- Put dialogue templates (`AMY_REPLIES`, scoring logic) in `pages/speech-coach/` — use `@workspace/speech-coach`
- Change mic/playback lifecycle, retry architecture, or session coordination from features

## DO

- Consume engine APIs from UI (`useAmyVoice`, `useSpeechRecognition`, `evaluateCoachResponse`, `mergeCoachJourneySnapshot`)
- Add coaching phrases, celebrations, dashboards, analytics **above** the engine
- Run `pnpm run check:speech-coach-engines` before merging PRs that touch these areas

## Core engine changes

Require in PR: root cause, reproduction, why extension fails, risk assessment, regression test. See `docs/speech-coach-engine-freeze.md`.

Also follow: `.cursor/rules/amy-voice-ownership.mdc`
